--- Scope / parity ---
Surface = native WinUI 3 port of web/src/components/data-display/DriveScore.tsx: a purely presentational drive
score panel — a circular score gauge beside a four-row component breakdown (efficiency / speed discipline /
range preservation / trip length). New code (apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/shared-surfaces/):
  - DriveScore.Model.cs (WinUI-free): DriveScoreRegistration (slug=DriveScore), DriveScoreModel (the SI drive
    inputs: DistanceM/DurationS/MaxSpeedMps/StartBatteryPct/EndBatteryPct), DriveScoreBreakdown,
    DriveScoreComponent, DriveScoreDisplay, DriveScoreProjection (the web computeDriveScore + getScoreColor port
    + i18n + bar/gauge/accessible-name assembly), and PII-safe DriveScoreDiagnostics (view.opened slug=DriveScore).
  - DriveScore.cs: a ContentControl that renders the TsGlassPanel -> [radial gauge] + [breakdown bars] and binds
    to the projection; the view performs no HTTP.
  - TeslaSync.App.Tests/SharedSurfaces/DriveScoreTests.cs: 41 headless tests (computeDriveScore vectors,
    getScoreColor thresholds, i18n keys/fallbacks, projected rows, gauge fraction + accessible names, model
    factory, diagnostics, arg guards).
Parity decisions (web source is THE spec):
  - Pure, synchronous, prop-driven ({ drive }); the parent Drive row/header owns any fetching => no fetch-driven
    loading/error/stale/offline chrome. The single populated branch (gauge + breakdown) ALWAYS renders; an absent
    SI field falls back to the same default the web uses, so the surface is never blank. Same precedent as the
    accepted shared-surfaces ScoreBadge (0078) and BatteryDelta (0077).
  - computeDriveScore ported term-for-term: SI fallbacks (distance/duration 0; maxSpeed -> avg speed;
    startBattery -> 100; endBattery -> start); four weighted components (efficiency 0-40 toward the optimal
    150 Wh/km, speed discipline 0-20 from avg/peak ratio, range preservation 0-20 from %/km, trip length 0-20
    plateauing at 50 km); total = clamp(sum,0,100). JS Math.round reproduced as floor(x+0.5) (exact for the
    finite non-negative score domain, e.g. 12.5 -> 13). Vectors cross-checked against a faithful JS replica:
    {} -> 23/13/10/0/0; good(50km) -> 87/40/9/18/20; warn(30km) -> 53/13/13/15/12; bad(5km) -> 6/0/4/0/2;
    optimal(60km) -> 89/30/20/19/20.
  - getScoreColor thresholds: <40 => #ef4444 (web COLOR.BAD), <70 => #f59e0b (WARN), >=70 => #10b981 (GOOD).
  - Gauge drawn with the shared chart geometry the native radial gauges use: ChartGeometry.RingArc (12 o'clock,
    sweeping clockwise score/100) + ChartShapes.ArcPath (round caps = web strokeLinecap="round"). The arc + the
    centred score figure are tinted by the threshold palette via DisplayPrimitives.HexBrush (a semantic data
    colour shared with the web, like the ScoreBadge A-F palette; ambient theming still flows through the token
    brushes). Background ring = TsColorBorderBrush (web --glass-border). Breakdown bar palette (efficiency
    #00f0ff, speed #a855f7, range #10b981, trip #f59e0b) via HexBrush; bar track = TsColorBorderBrush; all text
    via the W1 token brushes (TextPrimary/Secondary/Muted).
  - Motion: the web framer-motion entrance (the arc drawing in via strokeDashoffset, the score figure fading in,
    the bars growing from zero) is reproduced once on Loaded as an XAML Storyboard (StrokeDashOffset draw +
    Opacity fade + ScaleX grow). Reduced-motion-aware: under MotionPreference.ReduceMotion the gauge/score/bars
    snap to their settled state with no entrance (web prefers-reduced-motion short-circuit). The data-bearing
    final visual is always composed in Render(), so every host (incl. reduced-motion) shows the complete surface.
  - i18n: the six web keys (driveScore.title, .score, .efficiency, .speedDiscipline, .rangePreservation,
    .tripLength) resolve through the P1/S10 ILocalizer facade (PassthroughLocalizer in tests) with the exact keys
    + English fallbacks. All six ALSO exist in the shared catalog Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw (as
    translation.driveScore.*) with the matching English values — verified present in all three locales.
  - a11y: the gauge reads as ONE Narrator node ("Score {total}"); the panel title is a level-3 heading (web h3);
    each breakdown bar carries a composed accessible name ("{label} {value} / {max}"); the decorative ring/arc
    and the inner score/caption figures are AccessibilityView.Raw. No interactive elements exist on this surface.

--- Tests-project registration (no corruption to repair on this branch) ---
TeslaSync.App.Tests is plain net10.0 and cannot project-reference the WinUI app, so each WinUI-free surface source
is Compile-linked. Added the new SharedSurfaces\DriveScore.Model.cs link in case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted
position (between DraftRestorePrompt.ViewModel.cs and EditConflictBanner.Model.cs), preserving the file's single
<Project>/<ItemGroup> invariant. The bare WinUI view DriveScore.cs is intentionally NOT linked (exercised by the
app build), matching the ScoreBadge/BatteryDelta linking pattern. The csproj was valid single-root on this branch
(no merge=union corruption to regenerate). New surface .cs files were authored with CRLF and converted to LF to
satisfy the repo .editorconfig (end_of_line = lf); see FORMAT step.

