--- UIAutomation E2E capability note ---
TeslaSync.App.UITests (Category=UIAutomation, 147 tests) drives the PACKAGED app out-of-process over the W3C
WebDriver protocol via WinAppDriver/Appium. This runner has no WinAppDriver/Appium listener (port 4723) and no
deployed MSIX, so the suite fails fast BY DESIGN (the csproj + WinAppDriverSession state it is never silently
skipped). These are repo-wide app-shell E2E tests, NOT part of this surface (this surface adds ZERO UIAutomation
tests; its required adapter/per-state/a11y tests are the 41 headless tests above). The required surface
capability (WinUI 3 / WindowsAppSDK 2.1.0 / .NET 10) IS present: the solution builds Release-clean and the
headless suite is fully green. Per the UITests csproj, the headless and UIAutomation suites run independently;
the headless result is the surface gate. The 147 UIAutomation failures are an environment/runner-infra gap, not
a defect, and match the accepted shared-surfaces BatteryDelta (0077) gate.

